  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women for Women&apos;s Human Rights 2016-2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Women for Women&apos;s Human Rights 2016-2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to WWHR-New Ways Association to train women on women&apos;s human rights and support gender equality with lobbying and advocacy.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen avser k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till Women for Women Human Rights (WWHR) New Ways Association som utbildar kvinnor om kvinnors m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och arbetar f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kad j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet genom lobbying och opinionsbildning.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main target of WWHR is to support the active and broad participation of women in the establishment and maintenance of an egalitarian and peaceful social order at national, regional and international levels through a rights-based approach to promote women&#x2019;s human rights in Turkey and abroad. - Description/Theory of Change In line with above mission, WWHR believes sustainable change results from:&#x2022; Capacity building through training and support programs such as Women&apos;s Human Rights Education Programme(HREP), International Sexual and Bodily Rights Institutions, working groups, seminars, etc.&#x2022; Networking and coalition building at different levels of the women&#x2019;s movement and other rights-based movements.&#x2022; Joint advocacy towards legal reforms and their implementation as well as the reinforcement of international policies and norms.&#x2022; Production and Sharing of Feminist Knowledge: Documentation and promotion of feminist discourses and strategies;</narrative>
  </description>
